\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Model 3 --- pro-dancer judge-appeal vs.\ fan-appeal biplot, with the six largest $|\Delta _p|$ professionals annotated. Read with the run's caveat: the judge-side effects were degenerate (all $\theta ^J_p = 0$) in the as-executed configuration, so the judge axis carries no information; the fan-appeal spread reflects genuine between-pro dispersion in fan support.}}{23}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:m3biplot}{{10}{23}{Model 3 --- pro-dancer judge-appeal vs.\ fan-appeal biplot, with the six largest $|\Delta _p|$ professionals annotated. Read with the run's caveat: the judge-side effects were degenerate (all $\theta ^J_p = 0$) in the as-executed configuration, so the judge axis carries no information; the fan-appeal spread reflects genuine between-pro dispersion in fan support}{figure.caption.14}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Model 3 --- trait-effect forest plot, judge equation vs.\ fan equation, with 95\% credible intervals. Every interval spans zero: celebrity age and industry have no reliably estimable effect on either audience at this sample size.}}{24}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:m3forest}{{11}{24}{Model 3 --- trait-effect forest plot, judge equation vs.\ fan equation, with 95\% credible intervals. Every interval spans zero: celebrity age and industry have no reliably estimable effect on either audience at this sample size}{figure.caption.15}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Model 3 --- fairness vs.\ mean upset rate over the $(\omega ,\tau )$ grid, colored by $\omega $ (judge weight). The frontier is monotone: judge-only weighting ($\omega = 1$) achieves $\approx 0.999$ merit protection with near-zero upsets, while fan-only weighting ($\omega = 0$) produces upsets in $\approx 96\%$ of simulated weeks. The recorded ``optimum'' at $\omega =0$ is a column-semantics artifact (corrected in the text); the suspense bonus $\tau $ adds no identifiable effect.}}{25}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:m3pareto}{{12}{25}{Model 3 --- fairness vs.\ mean upset rate over the $(\omega ,\tau )$ grid, colored by $\omega $ (judge weight). The frontier is monotone: judge-only weighting ($\omega = 1$) achieves $\approx 0.999$ merit protection with near-zero upsets, while fan-only weighting ($\omega = 0$) produces upsets in $\approx 96\%$ of simulated weeks. The recorded ``optimum'' at $\omega =0$ is a column-semantics artifact (corrected in the text); the suspense bonus $\tau $ adds no identifiable effect}{figure.caption.16}{}}
